<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>US Postal Service whistleblower warns new system could disrupt midterm election voting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc13c16ecfb9475541eee9eff5abe394f23d37f63b7b805c04f98ee6c0b4b900</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T03:48:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260902-us-postal-service-whistleblower-warns-new-system-could-disrupt-midterm-election-voting" /><summary type="html">A US Postal Service whistleblower has warned that a new ballot-processing system ordered by President Donald Trump and due to launch Tuesday could prevent millions of Americans from receiving mail ballots ahead of November's midterm elections.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Man accused of killing Charlie Kirk to face murder trial and possible death penalty</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:520e1652b3327ea0d9cabe36c7f0575eb72b32ff9bbfc1fc8caa1817c19cfe44</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T03:38:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260902-man-accused-of-killing-charlie-kirk-to-face-murder-trial-and-possible-death-penalty" /><summary type="html">A judge in the US state of Utah has ruled that the man accused of shooting far-right activist Charlie Kirk will face trial for murder. Tyler James Robinson, 23, is accused of fatally shooting Kirk in the neck during a rally at a Utah college campus in September 2025, allegedly because he was 'fed up' with the 'hate' Kirk spread.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>G20 backs final statement despite Russia tensions, China dissent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea5dd448817be7d2df0e0b9660675d3982a52befe899f013a2cc151607f5fea5</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T23:39:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-g20-backs-final-statement-despite-russia-tensions-china-dissent" /><summary type="html">G20 finance leaders wrapped up two days of talks in Ashville, North Carolina, on Tuesday with broad backing for a final statement, despite tensions over Russia’s participation and divisions with China. US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said Moscow’s presence had not disrupted discussions, as ministers also grappled with the war in the Middle East, tariffs, global trade imbalances and continued support for Ukraine.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Google Maps changes Lake Ontario to ‘Lake America’ as MapQuest downloads surge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c3000a2f8a88c5a64ec7dbd2a3e95e0eee702200a7a529fbaee60f066245b6f</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T19:37:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/2026-09-01-18-44-yes-google-maps-renamed-lake-ontario-as-lake-america" /><summary type="html">Lake Ontario is now appearing as “Lake America” on Google Maps for US users, following Donald Trump’s executive order to rename the lake. Canadians still see “Lake Ontario”, while users elsewhere see both names. But the change is far from universal: Apple Maps and MapQuest continue to use Lake Ontario. MapQuest has remained defiant against the move and since surged to the top of the US App Store download charts.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>AI data centers become surprise issue in US midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57e3a76caf9d763f291053d91876d8a8c1c14a6f41302f08fbd7d45b791567a5</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T19:35:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ai-data-centers-become-surprise-issue-in-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">The boom of data centers to power artificial intelligence was a topic of discussion at the G20 summit on Tuesday in North Carolina. Elon Musk told member countries that US companies need to find new energy sources outside of China to power these massive data centers. That same issue is also creating a backlash in the United States ahead of the midterm elections in November. Donald Trump is doubling down, calling those who are against the data centers, “backwards and poor.” FRANCE 24's Monte Francis explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>US firm to take over some Venezuela oilfields previously run by Chinese, Russian firms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81ca7652adca81e7002ad36357ceba66d545236845e70e59b4aedc233bfd216c</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T19:00:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-firm-to-take-over-some-venezuela-oilfields-previously-run-by-chinese-russian-firms--d77ac727647b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-firm-to-take-over-some-venezuela-oilfields-previously-run-by-chinese-russian-firms" /><summary type="html">The White House on Monday said it’s partnering with North American Blue Energy Partners as part of President Donald Trump’s push to tap into Venezuela’s oil industry, setting up a deal that will give the Pentagon a stake over roughly a fifth of the country’s vast oil reserves. Venezuela's ruling party-dominated ​National Assembly backed the ​country's oil deal with the Trump administration in a vote on ​Tuesday. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lindsay Clancy: The trial putting postpartum mental illness in the spotlight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d4e1838242bb3737ce6c1c3408d420b370bc0710a656e66780e5d5f58557a52</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T17:11:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-lindsay-clancy-the-trial-putting-postpartum-mental-illness-in-the-spotlight--22bc7aec8147.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-lindsay-clancy-the-trial-putting-postpartum-mental-illness-in-the-spotlight" /><summary type="html">Jurors in the murder trial of Lindsay Clancy notified the judge ​on September 1 that they were unable to reach a unanimous decision on whether to convict her for killing her three young children at her home in ​2023 – a ‌tragedy her attorney contends occurred while she was suffering ⁠from postpartum psychosis. FRANCE 24 takes a closer look at this case, which has sparked fevered debate in the United States over postpartum mental health.</summary></entry><entry><title>Alejandro Betancourt, the controversial Venezuelan oil tycoon Trump is banking on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2eb497be6d40882ffaa91024b67e761f326407a036f86e3a644dd9adcc51c45d</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T15:05:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-alejandro-betancourt-the-controversial-venezuelan-oil-tycoon-trump-is-banking-on--c93cd06358d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-alejandro-betancourt-the-controversial-venezuelan-oil-tycoon-trump-is-banking-on" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Friday announced "the biggest oil deal in world history" – a new deal with Venezuela for "65 billion barrels of oil". Washington is set to take a 35 percent stake in North American Blue Energy Partners, which is owned by controversial Venezuelan oil tycoon Alejandro Betancourt.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Controversial designer John Galliano cancels Met exhibition after backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:845f3cee6c9ebef48733cff7b619e49d39d306c0846f5b14043a6dee5278ed90</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T14:28:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/controversial-designer-john-galliano-cancels-met-exhibition-after-backlash--bfcd67c2a6d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/controversial-designer-john-galliano-cancels-met-exhibition-after-backlash" /><summary type="html">John Galliano has cancelled an upcoming major exhibition celebrating his work as a fashion designer after it prompted criticism due to his previous conviction for making antisemitic remarks. In 2011, a French court found the designer guilty of antisemitic and racist rants at a Parisian bar. He was also fired by Dior as creative director that same year after a video surfaced of him declaring a love for Hitler.</summary></entry><entry><title>Jury convicts former gang member of rapper Tupac Shakur's murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2aee127f72cf420ec7b93ff44cbaa8435f304303a585c40f99a8c489a0f86f7b</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:52:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/jury-convicts-former-gang-member-of-rapper-tupac-shakur-s-murder--82a05ff01328.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/jury-convicts-former-gang-member-of-rapper-tupac-shakur-s-murder" /><summary type="html">Twelve jurors found former gangster Duane "Keffe D" Davis guilty of the murder of Tupac Shakur in Nevada's Clark County court on August 31. Although the 63 year-old is not thought to have fired the deadly shots himself, he is the only man still alive out of those who were in the car at the time. Under Nevada law, someone who helps another person commit murder can be convicted of the crime.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's G20 US invitation severely criticised by European countries</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5f2428326fe97b8324c5741638b738d536db5fe5b4870a0b6d479c1a537786d</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:48:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-s-g20-us-invitation-severely-criticised-by-european-countries--bc062679808d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-g20-us-invitation-severely-criticised-by-european-countries" /><summary type="html">Finance ministers and central bank governors from the group of 20 major economies are meeting for two days in Asheville, North Carolina. With the United States holding the rotating G20 presidency, Washington is trying to rally partners towards greater economic pressure on Iran and find ways to boost growth. But an unexpected attendee drew fierce criticism.</summary></entry><entry><title>Former gang member found guilty of murdering rapper Tupac Shakur</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6bfcc80be30f779e32440d22ba95fc2e7af646bdf1d38543d138f16411c27b03</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:31:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/former-gang-member-found-guilty-of-murdering-rapper-tupac-shakur--948ee9415051.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/former-gang-member-found-guilty-of-murdering-rapper-tupac-shakur" /><summary type="html">A jury found Duane “Keffe D” Davis guilty of orchestrating the 1996 killing of rap icon Tupac Shakur, finally bringing a measure of resolution to a case that had gripped hip-hop fans and lingered in the public imagination for decades. Davis could be sentenced to life in prison following that verdict. FRANCE 24's Wassim Cornet tells us more about the verdict.</summary></entry><entry><title>Government air strikes kill 20 alleged guerrillas in Colombia, president says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64ae28bd6f6ea548da67b4d83d687eb10914023a9313284f44e75e5d8725b9c2</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T05:42:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-government-air-strikes-kill-20-alleged-guerrillas-in-colombia-president-says--2ea484196c10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-government-air-strikes-kill-20-alleged-guerrillas-in-colombia-president-says" /><summary type="html">Fresh government air strikes have killed 20 alleged members of the Central General Staff (EMC) armed group in southern Colombia, the country's new right-wing President Abelardo de la Espriella said Monday. The new administration carried out two other deadly air strikes against suspected guerrillas in August, which sources within Colombia's forensics authority say killed at least four minors.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Duane 'Keffe D' Davis found guilty in Tupac Shakur murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bd276ce562dc271b5222821bffa9f86041321e027a91fdf763bb770a8e9cd17</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T00:53:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-duane-keffe-d-davis-found-guilty-in-tupac-shakur-murder--2129e603d6d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-duane-keffe-d-davis-found-guilty-in-tupac-shakur-murder" /><summary type="html">Duane “Keffe D” Davis was found guilty Monday of orchestrating the 1996 murder of rap icon Tupac Shakur, becoming the first person convicted in the decades-old case. The 63-year-old faces a possible life sentence after a Las Vegas jury deliberated for less than three hours.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Fashion designer Galliano calls off Met Gala exhibit as backlash over anti-Semitic rant mounts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4f0935543d3399ac632075099f374556f1485b4ecad686b66846244cea4bed2</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T19:09:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260831-fashion-designer-galliano-calls-off-met-gala-exhibit-as-backlash-over-anti-semitic-rant-mou--0066b3984640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260831-fashion-designer-galliano-calls-off-met-gala-exhibit-as-backlash-over-anti-semitic-rant-mounts" /><summary type="html">A planned nine-month retrospective of the work of fashion designer John Galliano at New York's Metropolitan Museum of Art has been called off following backlash over the British designer's 2011 conviction for anti-Semitic and anti-Asian comments. Footage surfaced in 2011 showing Galliano hurling racist and anti-Semitic slurs at patrons in a Paris bar the previous year.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Colombian rebel group say kidnapped French Foreign Legion soldier is still alive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:120f1142547c70bbc3fc4840f6bbecb0ef55abe6717b39799d82972539a3d13a</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T09:54:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260831-colombian-rebel-group-say-kidnapped-french-foreign-legion-soldier-is-still-alive--f3a2a5dd9d90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260831-colombian-rebel-group-say-kidnapped-french-foreign-legion-soldier-is-still-alive" /><summary type="html">Rebels from the Central General Staff, the main splinter group of Colombia's defunct FARC guerrillas, on Sunday said they were responsible for kidnapping a Colombian national serving in the elite French Foreign Legion. The guerrillas said that Jose Olger Melo Charry, who was reportedly on leave in his home country, was alive and in "perfect health".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Vance to address Republican Jewish Coalition as activists raise concerns over anti-Semitism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30c42505780560599412677738de58e371d6591e14338a048647afaa4033f65a</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T07:05:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260831-vance-to-address-republican-jewish-coalition-as-activists-raise-concerns-over-anti-semitism--abfb17098ac8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260831-vance-to-address-republican-jewish-coalition-as-activists-raise-concerns-over-anti-semitism" /><summary type="html">US Vice President JD Vance will make a private address on Monday at the annual gathering of the Republican Jewish Coalition, a collection of conservative Jewish activists. Vance's more equivocal stance on Israel has been criticised by some pro-Israel figures within the conservative movement, who have also raised concerns over his refusal to distance himself from commentators such as Tucker Carlson, who have given a platform to far-right anti-Semitic figures.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Two dead and around 15 missing as flash flood strikes Grand Canyon National Park</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77566eab90f69c6d178c6f076f6ad996115fb456ab973705a4a1df135553b561</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T01:38:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260831-grand-canyon-national-park-flash-flood-missing--1b670bda7425.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260831-grand-canyon-national-park-flash-flood-missing" /><summary type="html">At least two people died and more than 15 people may be missing after flash floods struck Grand Canyon National Park in Arizona, the National Park Service said on Sunday. Flooding hit the Bright Angel Canyon and Phantom Ranch area on Saturday, prompting authorities to evacuate visitors and search for people who remain unaccounted for.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Treasury bars certain journalists from G20 meeting in North Carolina</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57a818485d55f442eb857ce9189145a422de2a9df1578fedcc68653a953069ea</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T22:48:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260830-us-treasury-journalists-from-g20--c140853c1da2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260830-us-treasury-journalists-from-g20" /><summary type="html">The US Treasury Department denied credentials to reporters from The New York Times, The Wall Street Journal and Bloomberg for a G20 finance meeting in North Carolina, the latest restriction on media access under US President Donald Trump. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said the decision was unrelated to journalists’ viewpoints.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says NBC journalist to be reported to FCC for ‘punishment’ over endorsement coverage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a22f96f249eaca77bfeed869a81cf7a3f418c61cbaadf0d731cc89582e44a547</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T17:06:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260830-trump-says-nbc-journalist-to-be-reported-to-fcc-for-punishment-over-endorsement-coverage--4b25e5d5d8c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260830-trump-says-nbc-journalist-to-be-reported-to-fcc-for-punishment-over-endorsement-coverage" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Sunday said prominent NBC anchor ​Kristen Welker will be reported to the Federal Communications Commission (FCC) for "rebuke or punishment" after she reported the Republican president had "mixed results" in his endorsement ​of candidates for the November midterm elections.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US and Venezuela seal 25-year oil deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ccbb4d4f9b8b9f3cc6c5a831c95a5e009f63e6cbe60d984112ae7418bffe1321</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T11:34:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-and-venezuela-seal-25-year-oil-deal--115b7ac2499b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-and-venezuela-seal-25-year-oil-deal" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump has called it “the biggest oil deal in world history”, while Venezuela’s interim president has assured the public that the country will retain control of its oil under the agreement. The “historic” 25-year deal with Washington involves 65 billion barrels of Venezuelan oil and aims to allow the country to develop its oil industry while preserving “ownership of and sovereignty” over its resources, Rodriguez said in a televised address. Rachael Griffiths has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Argentines march on Peter Thiel's mansion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4faba0bcd4db0da4327c9dc046213e691f0f432dcabe6c9d492158cfab3f8fd2</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T10:06:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/argentines-march-on-peter-thiel-s-mansion--3f2016b00340.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/argentines-march-on-peter-thiel-s-mansion" /><summary type="html">In Argentina, protesters marched toward a mansion reportedly purchased by American tech billionaire Peter Thiel. Activists accuse Thiel of seeking to profit from the country’s natural resources and wielding excessive political influence in the South American nation. Peter O'Brien reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>NASA launches Roman telescope to map 'a new atlas of the universe'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e2be43fb259f615410d8b9a77d209537b42107ae87e66f3d1b2b9457d05afb9</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T05:26:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260830-nasa-set-to-launch-roman-telescope-to-map-the-universe--328f7ccfda9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260830-nasa-set-to-launch-roman-telescope-to-map-the-universe" /><summary type="html">NASA on Sunday launched its Roman Space Telescope aboard a SpaceX Falcon Heavy rocket, beginning a multi-year mission to create a vast new map of the cosmos. With a field of view far wider than Hubble’s, Roman will search for exoplanets and supernovae while also probing two of the biggest mysteries in physics: dark matter and dark energy.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'I am sure of myself': A look back at Dolly Parton's unspoken feminist legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4de7d68516d31864c7ea371e656728426dd32ed9034512e5eb1f20ff6e5731f7</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T15:57:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260829-i-am-sure-of-myself-a-look-back-at-dolly-parton-s-unspoken-feminist-legacy--01fc466366c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260829-i-am-sure-of-myself-a-look-back-at-dolly-parton-s-unspoken-feminist-legacy" /><summary type="html">Beloved country star Dolly Parton was many things to her fans, including an actor, singer, philanthropist and entrepreneur. But after her death on Tuesday at the age of 80, some admirers are remembering her as something she never overtly claimed: feminist icon.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US to control one fifth of Venezuela's oil reserves, Trump says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8110b3163b20bc229a2057ab98db674f215f4bc3ca139b67bdc0f801f4910c03</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T08:55:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-to-control-one-fifth-of-venezuela-s-oil-reserves-trump-says--d87a883f245a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-to-control-one-fifth-of-venezuela-s-oil-reserves-trump-says" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump on Friday announced an unprecedented US push ​to take control of a fifth of Venezuela's vast oil reserves, betting that American companies can revive the OPEC nation's battered energy industry while delivering a new source of crude to help bring down US fuel prices.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump announces 'historic' agreement for US stake in Venezuela oil reserves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ba81b330e3aa243bf01d0dae166fe4731ceb91fc544ab76ca8bc54836fce393</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T00:05:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260829-trump-announces-historic-agreement-for-us-stake-in-venezuela-oil-reserves--3a977984c276.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260829-trump-announces-historic-agreement-for-us-stake-in-venezuela-oil-reserves" /><summary type="html">Washington and Caracas announced Friday that they had reached a “historic” oil agreement, under which the United States will take majority control of more than 65 billion barrels of Venezuela's reserves.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US-CANADA: Trump signs order renaming Lake Ontario to ‘Lake America’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d1f2420c7e5d709fb7ede06e5041f7bc300cb963dbdbb4c9dac4866ccda1cf9</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T12:16:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260828-us-canada-trump-signs-order-renaming-lake-ontario-to-lake-america--cbf662590e25.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260828-us-canada-trump-signs-order-renaming-lake-ontario-to-lake-america" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump signed an executive order on August 27 to rename Lake Ontario as 'Lake America', a change he said would take effect immediately. Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney took to X, writing the Great Lake's name will remain 'now and always'. The order comes after US-Canada trade talks collapsed last week, prompting the two longtime allies to announce tit-for-tat tariffs</summary></entry><entry><title>US : Tate brothers remain in jail as judge delays bail decision</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1be2d937f91a1be4240b277f4b8b885e87895d34bc3d2f647333951ca1bb826</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T09:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-tate-brothers-remain-in-jail-as-judge-delays-bail-decision--a7d914057a6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-tate-brothers-remain-in-jail-as-judge-delays-bail-decision" /><summary type="html">Andrew and Tristan Tate will remain in custody in Miami after a federal judge declined to rule on their bail request as they fight extradition to the UK, where they face charges including rape, assault, human trafficking and money laundering. The UK has until mid-September to submit its evidence to the US State Department, while the brothers continue to deny wrongdoing and claim their online personas were fictional.</summary></entry><entry><title>French Foreign Legion soldier kidnapped in Colombia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb2b17ebaa51cfde00382d8b8904a043078e4aec7e242d78a9a1ff8c281719e2</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T05:24:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260828-french-foreign-legion-soldier-kidnapped-in-colombia--e1c9b79a48e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260828-french-foreign-legion-soldier-kidnapped-in-colombia" /><summary type="html">Colombian military announced Thursday that a French-Colombian soldier from the French Foreign Legion was kidnapped in early August while travelling in the department of Narino. The kidnappers are believed to be members of the Estado Mayor Central, dissidents from the far-left FARC guerrilla group.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US military faces ‘beyond critical’ shortage of Patriot missiles in Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea086cde2b7dc37dc47e74eec06f7a4a58c815ed5a2c2322e9e90f2cff0dc3d0</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T21:41:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260827-us-military-faces-beyond-critical-shortage-of-patriot-missiles-in-europe--937a6a458748.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260827-us-military-faces-beyond-critical-shortage-of-patriot-missiles-in-europe" /><summary type="html">The US military is running critically low on Patriot missile interceptors in Europe as the war with Iran drains stocks, according to US and NATO officials. The shortfall is raising concerns about NATO’s ability to counter a potential Russian ballistic missile attack, though officials said no such assault is imminent.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
